From faff6a96355f53051493ce36039c31f612075c9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:14:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Finish removing the train/val split from the scoring path

Scoring a freshly trained full-pool trajectory still failed with a
pool_indices_sha256 / batch_size mismatch. Causes and fixes:

- Stale trajectory shadowing: the three per-seed locators (result_plots,
  transfer_d, comparison) preferred a parent checkpoints/trajectory.json over
  checkpoints/seed_<seed>/, so a manifest left by an older 90%-split run won.
  Add trajectory.locate_seed_dir (seed child wins) and delegate to it.
- batch_size conflation: score_subsets and transfer_d passed the scoring
  --batch_size (256) to resolve(), which checks the batch size the reference
  was trained with (128). Add --reference_batch_size (default 128).
- run_score_subsets.sh / run_transfer_d.sh now pass an explicit per-seed
  template, fail early if a seed has no trajectory, and pass
  --reference_batch_size.
- objective.TrajectoryScorer: include the pool fingerprint in the cached
  gbar key so a cache from the old pool cannot be reused.
- run_d_accuracy_correlation: pool_size was len - 10%; now the full set.
- Stale docs/docstrings (45000 pool, 90/10 split, ~19 sd) and tests whose
  budgets assumed a 45000 pool (4500 -> 5000, sd 19 -> 20.1).
- Tests for locate_seed_dir, old-pool-hash rejection, and the training vs
  scoring batch-size check.
